--- `.ok`, `.reason`, `.kind` and `.trace` of a value whose type says it
--- cannot fail are decided before the program runs: true, empty, empty, no
--- trace (typed-values decision 1). What is read for them is still read,
--- the same in both modes: a call that logs logs, and an index past a
--- list's end stops. (Compiled, the value read for them was skipped: the
--- call never ran and the index never stopped.) A value that can fail, and
--- a parsed value whose item is JSON's null, are asked as the program runs.

fn loud[x]
    log['called `x`']
    return x

n = 3
log[n.ok]
log[len[n.reason]]
log[len[n.kind]]
log[len[n.trace]]
xs = [1, 2]
log[xs.ok]
m = map[a = 1]
log[m.ok]
log[loud[4].ok]
log[len[loud[5].reason]]
r = float['x']
log[r.ok]
log[r.kind]
j = json['[1, null]']
log[j[0].ok]
log[j[1].ok]
log[xs[5].ok]
log['not reached']
